import mundane definition stdlib/divisibility/even
import mundane theorem    stdlib/divisibility/even-or-odd
import mundane theorem    stdlib/divisibility/not-both
import mundane definition stdlib/divisibility/odd

theorem quadratic-plus-four-times-odd-iff-even
  note        An integer is even or odd. If a = 2k, then a² + 4a + 5 is
              4k² + 8k + 5, twice 2k² + 4k + 2, plus 1. If a = 2k + 1, it is
              4k² + 12k + 10, twice 2k² + 6k + 5, which is even and so not
              odd.
  let a ∈ ℤ                                                           (H1)
  then a² + 4a + 5 is odd ↔ a is even

1.  a² + 4a + 5 is odd ↔ a is even
    both directions

    direction
    assume a² + 4a + 5 is odd                                         (D1)

    1.1.  a is even or a is odd
          mun:even-or-odd n := a

    1.2.  a is even
          cases, from 1.1

          case
          assume a is even, which is the claim                        (C1)

          case
          assume a is odd                                             (C2)

          1.2.1.  k ∈ ℤ. a = 2k + 1.
                  obtain k: mun:odd, from C2

          1.2.2.  a² + 4a + 5 = 2(2k² + 6k + 5)
                  algebra, from 1.2.1

          1.2.3.  a² + 4a + 5 is even
                  mun:even n := a² + 4a + 5, from 1.2.2

          1.2.4.  a² + 4a + 5 is not odd
                  mun:not-both n := a² + 4a + 5, from 1.2.3, contradicting D1

    direction
    assume a is even                                                  (D2)

    1.3.  k ∈ ℤ. a = 2k.
          obtain k: mun:even, from D2

    1.4.  a² + 4a + 5 = 2(2k² + 4k + 2) + 1
          algebra, from 1.3

    1.5.  a² + 4a + 5 is odd
          mun:odd n := a² + 4a + 5, from 1.4
